-Orbito-Ethmoid (NOE) Fractures: fractures involving the central upper face. They affect the nasal bones, medial orbital walls, and ethmoid bone, and often disrupt the medial canthal ligament and lacrimal system.", "runs": [{"text": "Naso-Orbito-Ethmoid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(NOE)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Fractures:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fractures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "involving"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "central"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "upper"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "face."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "They"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "affect"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "nasal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bones,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medial orbital walls, and ethmoid bone, and often disrupt the medial canthal ligament and lacrimal system."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1103"}}, {"id": "body-17961", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Palatal Fractures: Fractures of the hard palate, often associated with maxillary fractures.", "runs": [{"text": "Palatal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Fractures:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Fractures"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hard"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "palate,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "often"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maxillary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fractures."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1103"}}, {"id": "body-17963", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Initial Assessment & Emergency Management", "runs": [{"text": "Initial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Assessment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "&"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Emergency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17964", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Follow ATLS principles:", "runs": [{"text": "Follow"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ATLS"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "principles:"}]}, {"id": "body-17965", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Airway with cervical spine control,", "runs": [{"text": "Airway"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cervical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "spine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "control,"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17966", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Breathing,", "runs": [{"text": "Breathing,"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17967", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Circulation,", "runs": [{"text": "Circulation,"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17968", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Disability,", "runs": [{"text": "Disability,"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17969", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Exposure.", "runs": [{"text": "Exposure."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17971", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Facial fractures demand extra vigilance for airway compromise from bleeding, edema, or bone displacement. The airway can quickly be secured using nasal/oral airway adjuncts, intubation, or emergency tracheostomy as needed.", "runs": [{"text": "Facial fractures demand extra vigilance for airway compromise from bleeding, edema, or bone displacement. The airway can quickly be secured using nasal/oral airway adjuncts, intubation, or emergency tracheostomy as needed."}]}, {"id": "body-17972", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A thorough history from the patient is required. In emergency setting, AMPLE mnemonic is used in trauma history to quickly gather essential information about a patient's medical background during emergency assessment:", "runs": [{"text": "A thorough history from the patient is required. In emergency setting, AMPLE mnemonic is used in trauma history to quickly gather essential information about a patient's medical background during emergency assessment:"}]}, {"id": "body-17974", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "A – Allergies: Identify any known drug or food allergies (especially to antibiotics, anesthetics, or latex).", "runs": [{"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "–"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Allergies:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Identify"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "any"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "known"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drug"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "food"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "allergies"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(especially"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antibiotics,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anesthetics,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "latex)."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17975", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "M – Medications: Current prescriptions, over-the-counter drugs, anticoagulants (e.g., warfarin, aspirin), steroids, or herbal supplements.", "runs": [{"text": "M – Medications: Current prescriptions, over-the-counter drugs, anticoagulants (e.g., warfarin, aspirin), steroids, or herbal supplements."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17976", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "P – Past medical history: Includes significant illnesses (e.g., diabetes, heart disease, seizures), surgeries, previous trauma, bleeding disorders.", "runs": [{"text": "P – Past medical history: Includes significant illnesses (e.g., diabetes, heart disease, seizures), surgeries, previous trauma, bleeding disorders."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17977", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "L – Last meal: Important for anesthesia planning (risk of aspiration); also relevant in surgical timing.", "runs": [{"text": "L"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "–"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Last"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "meal:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Important"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "anesthesia"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "planning"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "aspiration);"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "also"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "relevant"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "surgical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "timing."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17978", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "E – Events/environment related to injury: Mechanism of injury (e.g., fall, assault, MVC), use of safety gear (seatbelt, helmet), loss of consciousness, alcohol/drug use, environmental exposures (e.g., smoke inhalation).", "runs": [{"text": "E – Events/environment related to injury: Mechanism of injury (e.g., fall, assault, MVC), use of safety gear (seatbelt, helmet), loss of consciousness, alcohol/drug use, environmental exposures (e.g., smoke inhalation)."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17980", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Imaging & Diagnosis", "runs": [{"text": "Imaging"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "&"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Diagnosis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1112"}}, {"id": "body-17981", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Dental CT (CBCT) or normal CT scans are the standard radiological investigation, especially with suspected midface or complex fractures; Plain X-rays may be adequate for isolated nasal or mandibular injuries. In case of isolated mandibular fractures OPG can suffice.", "runs": [{"text": "Dental"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(CBCT)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "normal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CT"}, {"text": " "}, {"t